ginal `div` element with an `onclick` event is replaced with a standard HTML button. Added accessibility attributes such as `aria-haspopup=\"true\"` and `aria-expanded=\"false\"` can be incorporated. The button's `onclick` event updates the `aria-expanded` attribute.\n\nTesting considerations include verifying language attributes, native button elements, and specific text content. Keyboard interaction tests focus on the button's focus state, Enter/Space key presses, and the behavior of the menu's visibility toggle. Checking that the existing content within the `nav` and `main` elements are still intact is important. The solution aims for clean, compatible code that fulfills all the requirements.\n\n\n","type":"thinking"}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a5b49d1-fef5-431d-8dae-005f10d0b292","uuid":"74433b91-ac72-4253-90a2-0b4793d9dd0d","timestamp":"2026-11-01T11:26:36.487Z","thinking_duration_ms":11676,"thinking_display":"updates"}
